<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smalolholder rises on local buying.</title>
<headline>Tea Smalolholder rises on local buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd rose 2.8 percent, or 50 cents, to 18.50 rupees on buying of 7,000 shares by retail investors in early Wednesday trading, brokers said.</p>
<p>The company's shares rose 2.9 percent on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;There is a rush for firms which are in the tea business directly or indirectly, because the sector is doing very well,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories processes tea bought from small-scale tea cultivators.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
